410: # ================================================================ #519 CLOSURE -- THE TILED WINDOWS
411: #  WHY THESE SESSIONS EXIST.  `M13_widthdecline' (ok = 0 -> if (bufdepth == 4) ok = 0;) and
412: #  `M14_lineardecline' (-> if (linear) ok = 0;) were MEASURED TOTAL ESCAPES of the 14-row and the
413: #  19-row instruments (killtable_20260910/M13_widthdecline.raw, M14l_lineardecline_vs19.raw).  They
414: #  are UNDER-declining mutants: where the added condition is false the unsupported type is PERMITTED
415: #  and the store below runs -- and because #519 deleted the random() fill, a permitted store writes
416: #  UNINITIALISED buf.  They escaped because EVERY declined row above drives MODE_YCRCB 0x12f0 or
417: #  MODE_RESERVED 0x1250, i.e. BUFDEPTH_32 on LIN_A, so both conditions are TRUE at every declined
418: #  cell and neither mutant is ever exercised where it differs.
419: #
420: #  THE CLOSURE, and it is a CLASS closure rather than a cell repair (two passes had found the same
421: #  shape twice).  The guarded body is the one statement
422: #      cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, tileptr + ofs, buf, bufdepth, MEM_WRITE, ...)
423: #  and it reads exactly two lvalues the mode word controls:
424: #      tlb_mode = (mode >> 10) & 7        -- selects the switch arm that ASSIGNS tileptr
425: #      bufdepth = 1 << ((mode >> 8) & 3)  -- the store's own LENGTH, and ofs via tilewidth
426: #  tlb_mode's reachable-to-the-store partition is {0 TLB_A, 1 TLB_B, 2 TLB_C, 4 LIN_A}: 3 and 5-7
427: #  take the BADMODE default, which RETURNS before the store, and >= 8 is impossible after `& 0x7'.
428: #  bufdepth's domain is exactly {1, 2, 4, 8}.  The rows above hold ONE of those sixteen cells,
429: #  (LIN_A, 4).  These sessions drive the OTHER FIFTEEN, declined.  With all sixteen present in the
430: #  declined set, NO predicate over tlb_mode and bufdepth alone can be false at every declined cell,
431: #  whatever its shape -- which is why the closure is stated over the DOMAIN and not over a list of
432: #  mutant forms.  MEASURED, not reasoned: table 3's M20..M27 are that claim's negative controls.
433: #
434: #  THE THREE TILES ARE DISTINCT ON PURPOSE (clause (f)).  re_tlb_a[0]/b[0]/c[0] are 0x8001/0x8002/
435: #  0x8003, so the destinations are physical 0x10000/0x20000/0x30000.  An accept cell therefore pins
436: #  WHICH array the mode word selected, not merely that something was written somewhere; a decode
437: #  that sent TLB_B's PUT to re_tlb_a would leave this window's paint intact and RED its accept cell.
438: #  Bit 15 of the stored halfword is the tileptr's bit 31 -- the "valid" bit horrible_getputpixel
439: #  tests -- so 0x8001 is not decoration: 0x0001 returns without writing.
440: #
441: #  READ IMMEDIATELY AFTER EACH OPERATION.  Every cell repaints its own destination, fires one 1x1
442: #  rectangle and loads the word back inside ONE stepped instruction block, so a cell's oracle
443: #  observes its own operation and nothing else.
444: RE_TLB_A_W = 0xb5001000       # CRIME_RE_TLB_A: one 8-byte store fills re_tlb_a[0..3], big-endian halfwords
445: RE_TLB_B_W = 0xb5001200
446: RE_TLB_C_W = 0xb5001400
447: TILE_A     = 0x8001           # tileptr = re_tlb_a[0] << 16 = 0x80010000 -> phys 0x10000
448: TILE_B     = 0x8002           # -> phys 0x20000
449: TILE_C     = 0x8003           # -> phys 0x30000
450: KS_A, KS_B, KS_C = 0xa0010000, 0xa0020000, 0xa0030000
451: MARK1, MARK2 = "0x519519", "0x519520"     # a register echo used ONLY to split the transcript
452: OP_SW_T1_A2 = 0xacc90000      # sw $t1, 0($a2)  -- opcode 0x2b, rs=$6 (a2), rt=$9 (t1)
453: 
454: def tiled_prologue(A):
455:     """The three TLB windows and the DE state that does not change between operations."""
456:     c  = store(A, RE_TLB_A_W, TILE_A << 48, op=OP_SD_T0_A3)
457:     c += store(A, RE_TLB_B_W, TILE_B << 48, op=OP_SD_T0_A3)
458:     c += store(A, RE_TLB_C_W, TILE_C << 48, op=OP_SD_T0_A3)
459:     c += store(A, DE_DRAWMODE, DRAWMODE_SOLID)
460:     c += store(A, DE_FG, FG_VAL)
461:     c += store(A, DE_XVERTEX_0, 0x00000000)
462:     c += store(A, DE_XVERTEX_1, 0x00000000)
463:     return c
