563: # ================================================================ #519 PASS-4 -- THE CLASS CLOSURE
564: #  WHY THIS BLOCK EXISTS.  Pass 2 measured SIX mutants scoring 59/59 on the instrument as it
565: #  stood -- zero red rows, six times -- each one writing uninitialised host stack into guest
566: #  memory (regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260911/).  They were three passes of ONE
567: #  shape: a decline conditioned on an input the rows hold at a SINGLE VALUE.  M13/M14 were that
568: #  shape on bufdepth and tlb_mode; M28 on color_mode; M30/M31/M32 on the tile index, M33 on y,
569: #  M37 on the foreground colour.  The rule forbids buying another cell, so this closes the CLASS.
570: #
571: #  THE ENUMERATION, from the function's own inputs rather than from a list of mutant forms.
572: #  The guarded store reads exactly four lvalues -- tileptr, ofs, buf, bufdepth -- and their
573: #  inputs, walked up only to the enclosing function boundary, are:
574: #      bufdepth    <- (mode>>8)&3                  domain {1,2,4,8}   CLOSED by the 16 cells
575: #      tileptr     <- tlb_mode, tile_nr, array     tlb_mode {0,1,2,4} CLOSED by the 16 cells
576: #      ofs         <- x, y, bufdepth, tlb_mode
577: #      buf         <- color_mode (arm), *color (value)
578: #
579: #  THE BOUND: tile_nr, tile_nr_x, tile_nr_y, xofs and ofs are NOT independent axes.  Each is a
580: #  pure function of (x, y, bufdepth, tlb_mode).  So "close every derived coordinate" IS "close
581: #  the pair (x, y)" -- two free variables, not an open-ended demand.
582: #
583: #  *** AND THE WORD "COMPLETE" DOES NOT BELONG HERE.  An earlier draft of this block said "the
584: #  complete free input set is therefore { x, y, *color, color_mode-within-default }" and that
585: #  claim is FALSE in two ways, both found by a read-only audit seat and both checked here. ***
586: #
587: #  EXHAUSTED -- every value in the reachable domain is driven, so no predicate over these alone
588: #  can be false at every declined cell, whatever its shape:
589: #      tlb_mode    {0,1,2,4}     4 of 4      (the other four return before the store)
590: #      bufdepth    {1,2,4,8}     4 of 4
591: #      color_mode  16 nibbles    16 of 16    (4 accepting arms + 12 reaching `default:')
592: #
593: #  SAMPLED -- driven at more than one value, which kills the measured single-value family, but
594: #  NOT exhausted, so a slice WITHIN a driven class can still escape:
595: #      x           {0, 4, 132} of 2048          y  {0,1} masked, of 128
596: #      *color      2 values of 2^32
597: #      tileptr     {0x10000,0x20000,0x30000,0x40000,0x50000} -- the TLB ARRAY CONTENTS, which
598: #                  the line above lists as an input to tileptr and which the superseded
599: #                  sentence then silently dropped.  This one matters most: tileptr IS the
600: #                  store's address operand, so by the 2026-09-09 flow test the array VALUE is
601: #                  as much a floor axis as the array CHOICE (tlb_mode) already is.
602: #      mode        the raw parameter.  Bits 0-3 and 13-31 are read by NOTHING in this function,
603: #                  and every mode word any row drives has low nibble 0.
604: #
605: #  WHAT THAT COSTS, stated rather than glossed: `if (ok || (tileptr & 0xfff00000))',
606: #  `if (ok || (mode & 1))', `if (ok || (x & 1))' and `if (ok || (y & 2))' are each predicted to
607: #  score 77/77 and each is reachable by one ordinary guest store.  They are DERIVED, not
608: #  measured -- no table has run them.  They are filed in killtable4_20260911/RESIDUALS.md.
609: #
610: #  WHY THEY ARE NOT REPAIRED HERE, and this is the honest boundary rather than a dodge: a slice
